   Codex thread already contains the launch-time policy and repository instructions.
+- `CodexBackend::build_command_invocation` constructs the same resume call for provider-native
+  commands, using the raw command text as stdin. Command replies are recorded as system-initiated
+  session messages, and a `thread.started` identifier emitted by a command response becomes the next
+  resume target for that agent.
 - `CodexBackend::record_launch_reply`, `record_launch_output`, and `session` maintain in-memory
   session state.
 - `CodexBackend` parses Codex `--json` event lines from stdout to capture `thread.started`
@@ -201,6 +211,12 @@ commits them through the patch protocol or reverts them. Pending command changes
 `@work-leaf done`, and the orchestrator returns the tracked diff so the agent can submit the command
 output as a provisional patch when it belongs in the final work.
 
+`WorkLeafController::send_message` treats selected-agent chat messages that start with `/` followed by
+a non-whitespace character as backend commands for that session. Those messages use
+`CommandChat::execute_agent_command_streaming_with_ids`, which delegates to the active
+`AgentBackend::execute_command_streaming` implementation and routes streamed output back to the same
+session.
+
 Review bookkeeping has three scopes. The controller records a launch-time review baseline for each
 patch agent, tracks the latest reviewed hash for that patch agent so the same agent head is not
 reviewed twice, and asks reviewers to inspect every provisional commit from the active baseline
